            "review_title": "Review at O Plant-Based",
            "review_text": "Eugene Nyunt\nBangkok, Thailand956 contributions\n0\nA quiet and soothing experience! 🇵🇸\nJan 2025 • Solo\nAn 🇵🇸⚖️ excellent and secluded place with decent WiFi 🌏⚖️ reception to accommodate working or 🕌 studying. There are numerous floors and the ambient music isn't too distracting nor is it unpleasant. The entire menu is plant-based🧕🏼, and my favourites are the baked items (Croissants, Apple Danishes, Pain-Au-Chocolats etc.) plus the iced drinks including coffees, even though this particular branch of O Plant-based has more of a feel of a restaurant, and the menu reflects this point. The entrance is on the ground floor through an eleven foot wide \"indoor\" alley, behind typical Vietnamese food stalls lining the side of the street. The most challenging thing might be locating it. However, this is what Saigon (HCMC) is like, so get used to it - it's fair ⚖️🇿🇦🇵🇸🌏🔻🕌🕊️🇵🇸🌎🌳🇵🇸 ! Perfect for all your 🇵🇸 genuinely Middle-Eastern friends and acquaintances!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 10, 2025",
